OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F307A1786918698
OL,3,CFour Renaissance classics stolen from
OL,4,CSicilian museum during Italian holiday
OL,6,FThieves have stolen four Renaissance
OL,7,Fclassics from a museum in Sicily
OL,8,Fduring an Italian national holiday,
OL,9,Flocal media reported.
OL,11,FThe thieves bypassed the alarm and
OL,12,Fsecurity systems on Saturday evening
OL,13,Fat the MuMe in Messina museum to make
OL,14,Foff with three of the five surviving
OL,15,Fpanels of the San Gregorio Polyptych,
OL,16,Fdated to 1473, as well as the double-
OL,17,Fsided panel depicting the Virgin Mary
OL,18,Fand the dead Christ in Pieta, which
OL,19,Fwas removed from an armoured display
OL,20,Fcase, the news agency LaPresse
OL,21,Freported.
OL,26,@zD@\qp
